  "style": {
    "id": "kintsugi",
    "name": "Kintsugi",
    "description": "Break and mend: a glossy celadon tea bowl on pale oatmeal linen in soft window daylight falls, cracks along a seeded fracture (weighted spherical Voronoi of warped surface directions, so each crack runs through the whole wall) and splays into a dozen-odd shards that tip outward, clink down on the cloth convex side down and rest; they rise along arcs and slot back home; then molten gold runs ALONG the seams from one pour point on the rim (a Dijkstra arrival field over the seam network, baked into a texture), glowing hot at its leading tip and cooling to a raised, glossy, slightly irregular gold bead, with a few chipped-out spots filled flush with gold. Seams are evaluated per fragment, so they stay crisp at any distance. Ends on a slow orbit with the gold catching the light. Shard landings, returns and every seam junction the gold reaches are sound cues from the same plan.",
